      en: "Phuthaditjhaba is a town in the Free State province of South Africa, originally established as the capital of the QwaQwa homeland in 1974. Located in the Maloti Mountains, it has a population of about 50,000. The town serves as a commercial and administrative hub for the surrounding area. The economy relies on agriculture (maize, livestock), tourism (due to proximity to Golden Gate Highlands National Park), and government services. Phuthaditjhaba has several schools and a major hospital. The mountainous terrain offers scenic views and opportunities for hiking. It is also known for its Basotho cultural heritage.",
