      en: "Ladysmith is a town in KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, founded in 1850 on the Klip River. With a population of about 65,000, it is famous for the Siege of Ladysmith during the Second Anglo-Boer War (1899-1900). The town is an agricultural centre (maize, livestock) and transport hub. Tourism is significant, with the Ladysmith Museum and Siege Museum. The nearby Drakensberg Mountains offer recreational opportunities. Ladysmith is also the birthplace of the acclaimed choral group Ladysmith Black Mambazo. The town's architecture reflects its Victorian and Boer history.",
