      en: "Empangeni is a town in KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, founded in 1851 near the coast. With a population of about 110,000, it is a centre for agriculture and forestry, particularly sugarcane plantations and timber processing. The economy is diverse, with manufacturing and services. Nearby attractions include the Enseleni Nature Reserve and the Richards Bay harbour. Empangeni has several schools and a hospital. The climate is subtropical, with hot, humid summers and mild winters. The town serves as a commercial hub for the surrounding rural areas.",
