      en: "Ulundi is a town in KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, historically the capital of the Zulu Kingdom. Located on the White Umfolozi River, it has a population of about 30,000. Ulundi is famous for the Battle of Ulundi (1879), which ended the Anglo-Zulu War. The town houses the Royal Palace of the Zulu monarch. The economy is based on agriculture (livestock, maize) and government services. Attractions include the Ulundi Museum and the Ondini Cultural Museum. Nearby, the Hluhluwe-Imfolozi Park offers wildlife viewing. Ulundi remains a cultural and historical centre for the Zulu people.",
