      en: "Komani was established as Queenstown in 1853 and renamed in 2016. The town is known for its hexagonal town plan, a unique urban layout designed by British governor Sir George Cathcart. The plan features a central hexagonal square with roads radiating outward. The town serves as a gateway to the Baviaanskloof Wilderness Area, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The local economy includes wool, mohair, and cattle farming. The population is around 65,000. The town also hosts the annual Komani Agricultural Show.",
